Edge-Computing Mission Readiness Score Algorithm
Unlike consumer fitness apps that rely on cloud servers, space health apps compute readiness locally on a tablet or onboard computer. The algorithm compares live wearable readings against an astronaut's 7-day rolling baseline to account for normal microgravity adaptation.
Core Scoring Weights (0–100 Scale)
• Heart Rate Variability (HRV – 35%): Measures autonomic nervous system recovery and stress. A drop below 85% of the astronaut's baseline lowers the score.
• Resting Heart Rate (RHR – 25%): Tracks cardiovascular strain and upper-body fluid shifts. An elevation of more than 5 bpm above baseline triggers a penalty.
• Sleep Efficiency & Duration (25%): Counters circadian disruption from 16 orbital sunrises per day. Scores drop if sleep falls below 7 hours or efficiency drops below 85%.
• Skin Temperature Deviation (15%): Detects early infection or immune suppression. Deviations greater than ± 0.5°C from baseline reduce readiness.
